$m$~being an integer.

Show, by means of the direct definition of the
definite integral, and equations \\Eq{(1)}--\\Eq{(5)} above, that
\\CenterLine{\\Itemp{(i)}}{$\\ds\\int_{-a}^{a} \\phi(x^{2})\\, dx = 2\\int_{0}^{a} \\phi(x^{2})\\, dx$,\\quad
